  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of the Asian Elephant Range States Meeting and the Workshop to update the Indonesian Elephant Conservation Strategy and Action Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to convene the first Asian Elephant Range States Meeting in over a decade and to update the Indonesian Elephant Conservation Strategy and Action plan which will expire in 2017. The meetings will be held back-to-back in Banda Aceh, Sumatra, Indonesia, and be hosted by the Government of Indonesias Directorate General of Nature Resources and Ecosystem Conservation (KSDAE) with technical support from IUCN/SSC; organizational and logistical support will be provided by Yayasan Resolusi Gajah Indonesia and the International Elephant Foundation. The events will encourage information flow and discussion among range states that will result in consensus of elephant conservation management strategies, including: current status, threats assessment, habitat fragmentation and loss; human-elephant conflict; transboundary issues; future collaborations; and the update to the strategy for the action plan for Indonesia to conserve its elephants.</narrative>
  </description>
